# cyberwise upstream manifest
#
# sha256 of every behaviour-bearing file in the family, as it shipped. This is
# the "truth" half of the upstream guard; the "intent" half is the change
# register, which lives in the user bundle and never in this repo.
#
# Wiki articles are deliberately absent. They are meant to grow, and guarding
# them would fill the register with noise inside a day.
#
# Hashes are taken over content with CRLF collapsed to LF and any UTF-8 BOM
# dropped, so a fresh clone matches whatever line endings git hands you.
#
# REGENERATE DELIBERATELY, and only when the change IS the new upstream:
#     skills\cyberwise\tools\New-UpstreamManifest.ps1
# A local customization you want to keep goes in the register instead:
#     . skills\cyberwise\tools\UpstreamGuard.ps1; Register-CwChange ...
